  "dash.devices_explain": "Other devices connected to your account without a password (via QR/numeric code). They last <strong>3 days</strong> and renew while you use them; if 3 days pass without activity, they close on their own. You can revoke any of them at any time.",
  "dash.notif_explain": "Enable browser notifications to get an alert when you receive a message or call, even if you're in another tab or app. The first time you enter the site we ask for permission automatically; here you can check the status or request it again if you blocked it.",
  "dash.notif_why": "Why is this needed?",
  "dash.notif_why_p1": "Without notifications, if you have the chat tab in the background you might not see that a message or call arrived until you return to the tab. With them enabled, the browser alerts you just like WhatsApp or Telegram. <strong>Note:</strong> this only alerts while the site tab is open (even minimized). If you close the tab entirely, the connection drops and whoever calls you will see \"not connected\"; fixing that case requires a separate Push server (pending).",
